From 32cf96d1c9d4a8cdda6f846e3bcd9b068c62a126 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "keepup[bot]" <keepup[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: route messages with the Decisions API behind a
 setting

The model router starts a headless agent whose only job is to call
select_category with one label from a fixed list. That is a label-picking
call, which is what OpenAI's Decisions API is for: it returns one choice
from a supplied list and a probability for each option.

With ROUTER_CLASSIFIER=decisions and an OPEN_AI_KEY, classifyWithDecisions()
asks gpt-6-luna first. classifyWithLLM() is unchanged and stays the fallback
when the chosen option's probability is under 0.70, the call fails or is
refused, or there is no key.

The log says which path answered: a fall back logs why before the agent runs,
and what the agent returned after it has, so a failed agent never reads as an
answer.

A "none" at or above 0.70 is final and means no rule matched, so the agent
isn't paid to repeat it. A "none" under 0.70 goes to the agent, because a
weak "none" can hide a rule that should have matched.

The default stays "agent", so nothing changes until a person switches it on.
The pinned openai SDK (4.95.1) has no decisions resource, so this calls the
endpoint with client.post.

Replay date: 6 Oct 2026, Decisions API beta.
Source: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/changelog
